  "body": "## Issue\nCloses #1037\nClaim: cloud/i1037-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1037-sonnet)\nReviewer model: pending (Opus, adversarial review to come)\n\n## What and why\n\n**Problem.** A plain YouTube link in a message is a bare underlined URL, and a tap opens it in the in-app Safari view (operator feedback, 2026-11-17, #1037).\n\n**Cause.** The reader only builds LOT-108 player placeholders for LOT-035 candidates; every other link is plain text routed by `HFRLinkRoute` to `SFSafariViewController`.\n\n**Change.**\n- `YouTubeLinkDetector` (HFRParsing): `youtu.be/<id>`, `youtube.com/watch?v=<id>` (`www.`, `m.`), `youtube.com/shorts/<id>`; `t=` start via the LOT-035 parser. A card is for an `a.cLink` that holds text only, whose text is its own address (a named link stays a text link), outside any table (quote, spoiler, code), and that is **not** a LOT-035 player candidate. Channels, playlists, handles and look-alikes are not videos.\n- `TopicHTMLBuilder` adds a card under the message text (the link stays). It reads as the pill « Vidéo YouTube · toucher pour lire » until `reader.js` has the thumbnail `https://i.ytimg.com/vi/<id>/hqdefault.jpg` (operator decision, option 2 of #1037; de-facto form, not documented by YouTube, recorded in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c with a header capture and in LOT-071 T9). The thumbnail is an ordinary image of the page: policy C, cookie-less client, no `Referer`, `RequestTimeout.standard`. Refused (images on tap), failed or late: the pill stays, no placeholder, no link text in its place.\n- Tap on the card, the pill or the link: new bridge message `videolink`; the app re-parses the address and opens it over `https` as a universal link only, then Safari (`ReaderLinkMenu` `.app(provider: .youtube)` path, same as the long-press entry). Never `SFSafariViewController`, a web view or the player sheet; start time kept. The long press is unchanged (#596).\n\n**Decision to check (reviewer, operator).** LOT-035 candidates (a link alone in a top-level paragraph) already get the LOT-108 placeholder and the player sheet, which the issue says stays unchanged. So they get **no** card, and the two never show for one link. If most plain links in real messages are such candidates, the cards will be rarer than the screenshot suggests; I could not measure it from here. Showing both for one link would be a one-line change in `YouTubeLinkDetector.cards`.\n\n**Wider than the issue's wording:** none. `MessageEmbedDetector` only gained a shared `isCandidate` helper (its behaviour is unchanged, tests green).\n\n## How it was verified\n- `swift test` in `Packages/HFRKit`: 2105 tests pass. `YouTubeLinkDetectorTests` (9 tests, 40+ cases) was seen red before the code (missing types) and green after; four mutations are each caught (embed candidates not excluded, tables not excluded, named links accepted, any path accepted).\n- `swiftlint --strict` on the repository: 0 violations; `node --check reader.js` ok.\n- App tests **not run here** (Linux, no Xcode); written with compiler rigour and checked by `compile-check`: `ReaderVideoLinkTests` (card markup, no card for a LOT-035 candidate, a named link or a channel; thumbnail loads through the cookie-less client and shows; 404 leaves the pill; images on tap request nothing; tap on the card and on the link: universal only then Safari, no `events.link`, no `events.video`; an app that takes the link stops there; `http` posted, `https` opened; a non-YouTube claim opens nothing; an open composer ignores the tap) and `ReaderBridgeMessageTests` (`videolink`). The LOT-108 tests are untouched.\n- Third-party proof: `curl -sI https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dQw4w9WgXcQ/hqdefault.jpg` gave `HTTP/2 200`, `content-type: image/jpeg` (2026-11-18, headers only).\n- Device check for #893: the three SP videos of the screenshot topic show thumbnails; a tap opens the YouTube app, Safari with the app removed; airplane mode shows the pill.\n\n## Checklist (AGENTS.md §9)\n- [x] Module boundaries respected (HFRParsing only imports HFRModels-free SwiftSoup/Foundation; nothing UI in HFRKit)\n- [x] Tests added/updated\n- [x] No secrets; no fixtures added\n- [x] Docs updated (LOT-071 T9 + amendment, HFR-PROTOCOL §6c); after the merge, #1037 is closed by hand with `Done in #PR (merged as <sha>)`\n- [ ] Author model: Sonnet 5.5 / Reviewer model: Opus (pending)\n- [x] Ledger: see below; the PR touches no ledger path\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-new\nSection: Reader\n| GAP-1037 | Plain YouTube link in a message | A plain YouTube link stayed a text link (a LOT-035 candidate got the player placeholder only); a tap went to the in-app browser. No thumbnail. | ParseMessagesOperation.m:238-300, LinkItem.m:149-158 @ 2440d79 | A plain YouTube video link (`youtu.be`, `youtube.com/watch`, `m.`, `shorts`; text is the address; not in a quote, spoiler or code; not a LOT-035 candidate) shows a thumbnail card under the text (`i.ytimg.com/vi/<id>/hqdefault.jpg`, policy C, cookie-less), or the pill « Vidéo YouTube · toucher pour lire » when it is refused or fails. A tap on the card, the pill or the link opens the YouTube app (universal link only), else Safari; never the in-app browser nor the player sheet. | #1037 | UX change | new UX: operator (2026-11-17) | b·operator |\n```\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGsgPLqiPs3VRihgjR)_",
